CX.update({
'aberdeenshire':dict(lic=(SC_LIC[0]+' <a href="'+AB+'" rel="nofollow">Apply or renew online through Aberdeenshire Council</a> (questions: stl@aberdeenshire.gov.uk). You need one licence per separately bookable self-contained unit; a group of yurts or lodges on the same land can get a multi-unit licence. The council says a garden cabin, a self-contained extension or a converted steading, barn or garage with its own access needs a secondary letting licence. You must display a public notice outside the property; objections can be made within 28 days. Documents to send: EICR (within 5 years), PAT certificate and gas safety certificate (both within 12 months), EPC (secondary lets), and evidence of buildings insurance plus public or property owners liability cover of at least £2m. The council will not process incomplete applications and has up to 9 months to decide. A renewal must be in before the expiry date, or you become a new host and pay the higher fee.',SC_LIC[1]+[AB0,AB]),
 ctrl=NOCA,
 levy=('No scheme proposed yet. The council ran an initial survey from 24 Jun to 22 Jul 2025 (767 responses, 65% not supportive) and said a formal consultation would follow; we found no formal consultation published as of 22 Oct 2026. VisitScotland lists Aberdeenshire as early engagement only.',['https://engage.aberdeenshire.gov.uk/you-said-we-did/news_feed/aberdeenshire-visitor-levy',VS]),
 fees=('Applies until 31 Mar 2027, by maximum guests. New home sharing or letting: £364 (1 to 2), £481.50 (3 to 4), £610 (5 to 9), £727.75 (10 to 15), £909.75 (16+). New secondary letting, and provisional licences for new builds or conversions: £481.50, £642, £813.50, £909.75, £1,006. Renewal home sharing or letting: £331.75, £433.50, £545.75, £652.75, £824. Renewal secondary letting: £433.50, £578, £738.50, £824, £920.25. Duplicate licence £53.50. Variation £107 and transfer £150 (the council page dates these to 31 Mar 2026). Fees are non-refundable.',[AB,'https://www.aberdeenshire.gov.uk/licensing/licences-and-permits/stl-transfers-and-variations']),
 dates=['24 Jun to 22 Jul 2025: initial visitor levy survey','31 Mar 2027: current licence fees end']),
'dumfries-and-galloway':dict(lic=(SC_LIC[0]+' <a href="'+DG+'" rel="nofollow">Apply through Dumfries and Galloway Council</a> (shorttermlets@dumgal.gov.uk). Send a floor plan showing room sizes and bedroom occupancy, stairs or lifts, the use of each room, fire escape routes, any accessible rooms, smoke and heat detectors, and CO detectors if there is an open-flue appliance. Applications go on the public register and anyone can object during the 21-day notice period. Renewals are every 3 years and the council sends a reminder 3 months before expiry. The council says operating without a licence is a criminal offence, with a fine of up to £2,500 and a one-year ban from applying.',SC_LIC[1]+[DG,'https://www.dumfriesandgalloway.gov.uk/housing/landlords/property-licensing/short-term-lets']),
 ctrl=NOCA,
 levy=('No levy: plans dropped. After early engagement (29 Sep to 21 Nov 2025), the council\'s economy and infrastructure committee voted 10 to 8 on 9 Jun 2026 to stop all work on a visitor levy, with no formal consultation. Any future proposal would have to start again. (VisitScotland\'s list still showed Dumfries and Galloway under early engagement when we checked on 22 Oct 2026.)',['https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c621mp15zpno','https://www.dumfriesandgalloway.gov.uk/visitorlevy']),
 fees=('3-year licence, by maximum guests. Home sharing and home letting: £324 (up to 6), £361 (7 to 12), £413 (13+). Secondary letting: £357, £397, £454. The council says new, renewal and provisional applications currently cost the same. From 1 Apr 2026: confirming a provisional licence £79, transfer £79. Fees are non-refundable.',[DG]),
 dates=['29 Sep to 21 Nov 2025: visitor levy early engagement','1 Apr 2026: confirmation and transfer fees','9 Jun 2026: visitor levy plans dropped']),
})
