CX.update({
'east-renfrewshire':dict(lic=(SC_LIC[0]+' <a href="'+ERA+'" rel="nofollow">Apply online to East Renfrewshire Council</a> (the Private Sector Housing team runs the scheme). Read the council\'s checklists first: the online form cannot be saved part-way, and it takes one upload per evidence item (send extras to STL@eastrenfrewshire.gov.uk with the address and applicant name). All owners, day-to-day managers and the applicant go on one form, and the council checks title deeds. You get a provisional licence number, usually within 5 working days; once all documents and the fee are in, the council aims to decide within 28 days (the legal maximum is 9 months). Display the council\'s public notice at or near the property for 21 days from the day you apply (objections can be made for 28 days), then send the certificate of compliance to STL@eastrenfrewshire.gov.uk. Licences last up to 3 years. The council adds its own conditions to every first licence, covering hot tubs (a separate legionella risk assessment), antisocial behaviour, waste, key boxes and, for some flats, floor coverings and no arrivals or departures between 11pm and 7am. The council says it is revising its policy and portal, so for a transfer or a provisional licence for a new build, contact STL@eastrenfrewshire.gov.uk or 0141 577 8362.',SC_LIC[1]+[ERS,ERA,ERQ,ERC]),
 ctrl=(NOCA[0]+' East Renfrewshire says it does not intend to bring in a control area because short-term letting is estimated to be low, and it keeps this under review. Check with the council\'s planning service before you apply, telling them how often and for how long you will let: the council can refuse to consider a licence application if the let would breach planning control.',NOCA[1]+[ERS]),
 levy=('No levy, and no proposal found (searched 24 Oct 2026). East Renfrewshire is not on the national list of approved schemes and was not among the councils consulting on or considering a levy in a July 2026 Herald survey. Any Scottish levy needs at least 18 months\' notice. Separately, a December 2023 Cabinet report proposed removing the 10% second homes discount and charging a premium of up to 100% (double council tax) from 1 April 2024. <span class="tag warn">check with council</span> We could not confirm the final second homes rate on the council\'s website.',['https://visitorlevy.scot/visitorlevy/pages/levy-scheme',SLH,ERT]),
 fees=('From the council\'s fee table (read 24 Oct 2026; the page does not say which year it covers), by bedrooms, for a licence of up to 3 years. Secondary let: new £972 (up to 2 bedrooms), rising £53.50 per extra bedroom to £1,293 (8 or more); renewal £805 to £1,126. Home letting, or home letting and home sharing: new £661 to £982; renewal £549 to £870. Home sharing: new £377 (1 bedroom) to £483.40 (5 bedrooms); renewal £313 to £421. Provisional licence for a new build from £972, transfer £155; a material change of circumstances costs the same as a new application. The full fee is paid when you apply and is not refunded. <span class="tag warn">check with council</span> The table shows £962 (not £982) for an 8+ bedroom home letting and home sharing licence, so confirm that fee with STL@eastrenfrewshire.gov.uk.',[ERF,ERQ]),
 dates=['1 Oct 2022: licensing scheme opens','Dec 2023: Cabinet report proposes second homes premium from Apr 2024','Jul 2026: fee page last updated']),
'south-lanarkshire':dict(lic=(SC_LIC[0]+' <a href="'+SLK+'" rel="nofollow">Apply online through South Lanarkshire Council\'s licensing portal</a>, with the application checklist, the Scottish Fire and Rescue Service fire safety checklist, a copy of your EPC (where needed) and, for a new licence, eight copies of a layout plan showing escape routes, alarms, rooms, beds and occupancy. Police Scotland, Scottish Fire and Rescue, planning, building control, environmental services and housing are consulted, and local councillors are told. Once the council confirms your application is valid it sends you a site notice: display it at or near the property for 21 days, then sign the confirmation and return the whole notice to the Licensing and Registration Section (licensing@southlanarkshire.gov.uk). Objections go to the Licensing Committee. Licences last up to 3 years; apply to renew before yours expires and it carries on until the council decides (within 9 months). The council does not grant temporary exemptions. You can appeal to the Sheriff Court within 28 days. Fees are not refunded if you withdraw or are refused.',SC_LIC[1]+[SLK,SLG,SLP]),
 ctrl=(NOCA[0]+' South Lanarkshire\'s policy confirms there are no control areas in the council area, kept under review. Outside a control area a short-term let can still be a material change of use needing planning permission, decided case by case: speak to the planning service before you apply. If planning permission or a certificate of lawfulness is needed, it must go in with your licence application.',NOCA[1]+[SLP]),
 levy=('No levy yet. In October 2025 the Executive Committee agreed to research and informally consult on a possible visitor levy, after being told a 2.5% to 7.5% levy could raise £800,000 to £2.5 million a year. Researchers working for the council surveyed accommodation providers until 17 August 2026, and findings with a refreshed tourism strategy are due to go to councillors before any formal consultation. We found no formal consultation or decision (searched 24 Oct 2026). Any Scottish levy needs at least 18 months\' notice. Separately, the council\'s council tax page says second homes pay a 100% surcharge (200% council tax) from 1 April 2024.',[SLL,SLH,SLS,SLT]),
 fees=('Fees from 1 April 2026, by maximum occupancy (1 to 2 / 3 to 6 / 7 to 10 / 11 or more guests). The same fee applies to a new application, a temporary licence, a renewal or a variation. Secondary letting: £381.43 / £572.14 / £699.29 / £953.58. Home letting, home sharing, or both: £317.86 / £476.79 / £572.14 / £794.65. Provisional licence £200 (on confirmation you pay the full fee minus the £200), transfer £200, material change £50.85, duplicate licence £31.78, inspection fee to be agreed. Fees are non-refundable.',[SLF,SLG]),
 dates=['1 Oct 2022: licensing scheme opens','1 Apr 2024: second homes pay 200% council tax','Oct 2025: council agrees to research and informally consult on a visitor levy','1 Apr 2026: current fees apply','17 Aug 2026: levy research survey closes']),
})
import html as _h
def cfaq(c,x):
    nm=c['name'];tx=lambda v:_h.unescape(re.sub(r'<[^>]+>','',v)).strip()
    Q=[(f'Do I need a short-term let licence in {nm}?' if c['nation']=='Scotland' else f'Do I need a licence or registration for a short-term let in {nm}?',x['lic'][0]),(f'Do I need planning permission for a short-term let in {nm}?',x['ctrl'][0]),(f'Is there a visitor levy (tourist tax) in {nm}?',x['levy'][0]),(f'How much does a short-term let licence cost in {nm}?' if c['nation']=='Scotland' else f'What fees apply to short-term lets in {nm}?',x['fees'][0])]
    Q=[(q,tx(a)) for q,a in Q if a and tx(a)]
    ld=json.dumps({'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'FAQPage','mainEntity':[{'@type':'Question','name':q,'acceptedAnswer':{'@type':'Answer','text':a}} for q,a in Q]}).replace('</','<\\/')
    h=f'<h2>{e(nm)} short-let rules: quick answers</h2>'+''.join(f'<details><summary>{e(q)}</summary><p>{e(a)}</p></details>' for q,a in Q)+'<p class="small">Answers summarise the sections above. Follow each section\'s official source before acting.</p>'
    return h,f'<script type="application/ld+json">{ld}</script>'
ICO={'lic':'\U0001F4CB','ctrl':'\U0001F3D8','levy':'\U0001F4B7','fees':'\U0001F4B0'}
def sec(h,x,k=''):
    st='' if k=='fees' else '<span class="st yes">Registration required</span>' if 'must register' in x[0] else ('<span class="st no">None found</span>' if x[0].strip().startswith('No ') else '<span class="st yes">Applies</span>')
    return f'<section class="rc" aria-labelledby="rc-{k}"><div class="rch"><span class="ri" aria-hidden="true">{ICO.get(k,"")}</span><h2 id="rc-{k}">{h}</h2>{st}</div><p>{x[0]}</p>'+(f'<p class="small rs">Source: {src(x[1])}</p>' if x[1] else '')+'</section>'
def WHAT(c):
    import datetime as _d
    m=[ch for ch in d['changes'] if c['name'].split(' (')[0].replace('City of ','').replace(' City','') in ch['text'] and not ch['text'].startswith('Added')]
    if m:
        ch=max(m,key=lambda z:z['date']);dd=_d.date.fromisoformat(ch['date']).strftime('%-d %b %Y')
        return f'<p class="what"><b>What changed ({dd}):</b> {e(ch["text"])} <a href="{e(ch["source"])}" rel="nofollow">Source</a> · <a href="#alerts">Get alerts</a></p>'
    return f'<p class="what"><b>Last checked {_d.date.fromisoformat(C).strftime("%-d %b %Y")}:</b> no change logged for this council in our <a href="../changes.html">changes log</a>. <a href="#alerts">Get alerts</a> when it changes.</p>'
made=[];skipped=[]
for c in d['councils']:
    s=slug(c)
    if s not in CX or not c['verified']:skipped.append(c['name']);continue
    x=CX[s];dt=' '.join(reversed(C.split('-')));import datetime;dt=datetime.date.fromisoformat(C).strftime('%-d %b %Y')
    t=f'Short-term let rules in {c["name"]} (updated {dt})'
    kd=''.join(f'<li>{k}</li>' for k in x['dates']) or '<li>None listed.</li>'
    CF=cfaq(c,x)
    b=WHAT(c)+f'<p class="lead">{e(c["rule"])}</p>'+'<div class="rcs">'+sec('Licensing or registration',x['lic'],'lic')+sec('Control area / planning',x['ctrl'],'ctrl')+sec('Visitor levy',x['levy'],'levy')+sec('Fees',x['fees'],'fees')+'</div>'+(f'<h2>Scotland tools</h2><ul><li><a href="../scotland-short-term-let-licence-guide.html">How to get a short-term let licence (steps and checklist)</a></li><li><a href="../scotland-business-rates-checker.html">Business rates or council tax? 140/70 nights checker</a></li><li><a href="../short-term-let-fire-safety-scotland.html">Fire safety for short-term lets (alarms, doors, checklist)</a></li><li><a href="../uk-visitor-levy-map.html">Visitor levy map</a></li></ul>' if c['nation']=='Scotland' else '<h2>England guides</h2><ul><li><a href="../holiday-let-fire-safety-england.html">Holiday let fire safety in England: what you need and a checklist</a></li><li><a href="../england-second-homes-council-tax-premium.html">Second homes council tax premium: who pays, business rates and exceptions</a></li><li><a href="../occupancy-threshold-tracker.html">Business rates or council tax? Occupancy threshold tracker</a></li><li><a href="../holiday-let-tax-after-fhl-abolition.html">How holiday lets are taxed since the FHL regime ended</a></li></ul>' if c['nation']=='England' else '<h2>Wales guides and tools</h2><ul><li><a href="../wales-registration-checker.html">Do I need to register with the WRA? 4-question checker</a></li><li><a href="../wales-second-homes-council-tax-premium.html">Second homes council tax premium in Wales: rates, the 182-night test and exceptions</a></li><li><a href="../occupancy-threshold-tracker.html">Business rates or council tax? Occupancy threshold tracker</a></li><li><a href="../holiday-let-fire-safety-wales.html">Holiday let fire safety in Wales: what you need and a checklist</a></li><li><a href="../holiday-let-tax-after-fhl-abolition.html">How holiday lets are taxed since the FHL regime ended</a></li></ul>' if c['nation']=='Wales' else '')+f'<h2>Key dates</h2><ul>{kd}</ul>'+CF[0]+f'<p><a href="../{ {"Scotland":"scotland","Wales":"wales","England":"england"}[c["nation"]]}.html">All {c["nation"]} rules</a> · <a href="../councils.html">All councils</a></p>'+ALERT(c['name'],'council:'+s,f' Prefer every {c["nation"]} change? <a href="../{c["nation"].lower()}.html#alerts">Get {c["nation"]} alerts</a>.')
    page(f'councils/{s}.html',t,b,desc=f'Short-term let licensing, control area, visitor levy, fees and key dates for {c["name"]}, {c["nation"]}, with official sources. Updated {dt}.',full_title=t,head=CF[1])
    made.append(s)
print('council pages',len(made),'skipped',skipped)

